"this category in your agenda and in the month view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2857
#, no-c-format
msgid "Resources"
msgstr "Ressorgas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2858
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This group allows you to assign a color to each resource. Select a resource "
"in the drop down list, and press the button to open the <guilabel>Select "
"Color</guilabel> dialog, allowing you to select the color for that resource. "
"<link linkend=\"config-main-views\">Depending on the view preferences</"
"link>, this color will be used to mark events and to-dos which are stored "
"using this resource in your agenda and in the month view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2872
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Fonts"
msgid "Fonts page"
msgstr "Poliças"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2877
#, no-c-format
msgid "Time bar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2878
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press this button to pick the font, font style and size for the time bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2883
#, no-c-format
msgid "Month view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2884
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press this button to pick the font, font style and size for the month view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2889
#, no-c-format
msgid "Agenda view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2890
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press this button to pick the font, font style and size for the agenda view "
"(day, week and work week views)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2895
#, no-c-format
msgid "Current-time line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2896
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Press this button to pick the font, font style and size for the Marcus Bains "
"line (a red line in the agenda view indicating the current time)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2913
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use Groupware Communication"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2914
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this box to automatically send mails when creating, updating or "
"deleting events or to-dos which involve others. This mail can be an "
"invitation to attendees of an event you created, a cancellation of an event "
"you created, an answer or an update on your invitation status, an event "
"change request, &etc; Check this option if you you want to use the groupware "
"functionality (&eg; Configuring &kontact; as a &kde; <guilabel>Kolab</"
"guilabel> client)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2924
#, no-c-format
msgid "Send copy to owner when mailing events"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2925
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you check the <guilabel>Send copy to owner when mailing events</"
"guilabel> box, you will get a copy of all email messages that &korganizer; "
"sends at your request to the event attendees."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2931
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mail transport"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2932
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can choose which type of mail transport you would like to use. You "
"can either use &kmail; or the &Sendmail; command (which must be installed on "
"your system in order to work)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2938
#, no-c-format
msgid "Additional email addresses"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2939
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tells &korganizer; what further email addresses you have. You can add, "
"edit or remove additional emails addresses. These email addresses are the "
"ones you have in addition to the one set in <link linkend=\"config-main-"
"general-personal\">personal preferences</link>. If you get an invitation to "
"an event, but use another email address there, you need to list this address "
"here so &korganizer; can recognize it as yours, and add the item to your "
"calendar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3005
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Publish Tab</guilabel>: by publishing your free/busy information, "
"you allow others to take your busy time schedule into account when inviting "
"you to an event."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:3012
#, no-c-format
msgid "Publish free/busy information automatically"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3013
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enable this option if you wish your Free/Busy information to be uploaded "
"automatically. Note that you may skip this option and choose to mail or "
"upload your Free/Busy information via the <guilabel>Schedule</guilabel> menu "
"of &korganizer;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3018
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your application is setup to work as a <guilabel>&kde; Kolab client</"
"guilabel>, this is not required. The <guilabel>Kolab2</guilabel> server can "
"take care of publishing your Free/Busy information and manage the access to "
"it from other users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:3026
#, no-c-format
msgid "Minimum time between uploads (in minutes)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3027
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In case you choose to publish your information automatically, you may "
"configure the interval of time in minutes between each upload."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:3033
#, no-c-format
msgid "Publish (default 60) days of free/busy information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3034
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Configure the number of calendar days you wish to be published and available "
"to others"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:3039 index.docbook:3099
#, no-c-format
msgid "Server &URL;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3040
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the &URL; for the server on which your Free/Busy information shall be "
"published. Ask the server administrator for this information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3042
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Kolab2 server example: <userinput>webdavs://kolab2.com/freebusy/joe@kolab2."
"com.ifb</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:3048 index.docbook:3108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Username"
msgstr "Nom d'utilizaire"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3049
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the login information relative to your account on the server"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3050
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Kolab2 server specificity: Registered your UID (Unique IDentifier), by "
"default your UID would be similar to your email address on the Kolab2 server "
"but it may also be different. In the last case enter your UID. Ask about "
"your UID to the server administrator if you do not know it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:3057 index.docbook:3115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Password"
msgstr "Mot de pas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3058 index.docbook:3116
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter here your password (server login password)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:3062 index.docbook:3121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remember password"
msgstr "Se remembrar del mot de pas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3063
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this option if you want &korganizer; to remember your password and "
"skip asking you each time it upload your Free/Busy information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3066 index.docbook:3124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is not recommended to store your password in the configuration file for "
"security reasons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3072
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Retrieve Tab</guilabel>: by retrieving other peoples' free/busy "
"information, you can take their busy time schedule into account when "
"inviting them to an event."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:3079
#, no-c-format
msgid "Retrieve other peoples' free/busy information automatically"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3081
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Automate the process for retrieving other users free/busy time. Fill in the "
"server information section below to enable this option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:3087
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use full email address for retrieval"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3088
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This setting lets you change the name of the file which will be fetched from "
"the server. If you check this option, it will download a free/busy file "
"called <userinput>user@domain.ifb</userinput>, else it will fetch "
"<userinput>user.ifb</userinput>. Ask the server Administrator if you are not "
"sure about how to configure this option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3093
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Kolab2 server specificity:</guilabel> If you are configuring "
"&korganizer; as a component to a <guilabel>&kde; Kolab client (&kontact;/"
"Kolab)</guilabel> you have to check this option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the &URL; for the server on which your Free/Busy information shall be "
"fetched. Ask the server administrator for this information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Kolab2 server example: </guilabel><userinput>webdavs://kolab2.com/"
"freebusy/</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the login information relative to your account on the server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3122
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this option if you want &korganizer; to remember your password and "
"skip asking you each time it fetches the free/busy files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3134 index.docbook:3272
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plugins"
msgstr "Ajustons"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3136
#, no-c-format
msgid "For more information about configuring plugins, please refer to"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3145
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toolbars Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&korganizer; has four toolbars: a Main toolbar (with <guiicon>New Event</"
"guiicon>, <guiicon>New To-do</guiicon>, <guiicon>New Journal</guiicon>, "
"<guiicon>Back</guiicon>, <guiicon>Forward</guiicon>, <guiicon>Today</"
"guiicon>, <guiicon>Day</guiicon> and <guiicon>Week</guiicon> buttons), a "
"<guiicon>Views</guiicon> toolbar (for selecting between <guiicon>Agenda</"
"guiicon>, <guiicon>Month View</guiicon>, <guiicon>Timeline</guiicon>, "
"<guiicon>To-do List</guiicon> and <guiicon>Journal</guiicon> buttons), a "
"Schedule toolbar (with <guiicon>Publish Item Information</guiicon>, "
"<guiicon>Send Invitations to Attendees</guiicon>, <guiicon>Send Status "
"Update</guiicon> and <guiicon>Address Book</guiicon> buttons) and a Filters "
"toolbar, which allows you to choose a filter for the &korganizer; views and "
"manage the view filters as well. You can customize these toolbars in various "
"ways: you can add new icons, change the icon size, change toolbar position "
"and add text description to the icons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3163
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two ways to change the position of the toolbars:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can right click the toolbar to bring up the <guimenu>Toolbar Menu</"
"guimenu>. The icon size and text position can also be adjusted from this "
"menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a toolbar is unlocked, you can simply drag the toolbar by the handle on "
"the left border of each toolbar, and drop it whenever you wish. Also look at "
"other easy <link linkend=\"other-features-drag-and-drop\">drag-and-drop "
"operations</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3176
#, no-c-format
msgid "The toolbars are configured in two places:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The tool set is configured in the <menuchoice><guimenu> Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu "
"item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The graphic style (icon size, text position, &etc;) is adjusted through the "
"<guimenu>Toolbar Context Menu</guimenu>. Right click the toolbar to access "
"this menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure Toolbars Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This dialog allows you to customize the selection of tools on the toolbar. "
"Open it choosing the <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem> "
"Configure Toolbars...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3197
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choosing the toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First you need to choose the toolbar that you want to modify. All actions "
"apply to the toolbar that is selected from the drop down menu at the top of "
"the window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3205
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available Actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two rectangles below the toolbar title: <guilabel>Available "
"actions</guilabel> and <guilabel>Current actions</guilabel>. Using the left "
"and right arrows (located between the rectangles) you can move icons from "
"the <guilabel>Available actions</guilabel> group to the <guilabel>Current "
"actions</guilabel> group. The toolbar will have every icon that is in the "
"<guilabel>Current actions</guilabel> box. The up and down arrows allow you "
"reposition an icon."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remember that less icons may be better, because the screen is less busy and "
"therefore it is easier to find the toolbar buttons you actually use. For "
"instance if you always cut and paste with the keyboard hotkeys, you do not "
"need the <guiicon>Cut</guiicon>, <guiicon>Copy</guiicon> and <guiicon>Paste</"
"guiicon> icons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3224
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toolbar Context Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This menu allows you to change the look of the toolbars. <mousebutton>Right</"
"mousebutton> click the toolbar to access this menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3231
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Position"
msgstr "Posicion del tèxt"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Initially, icons have text alongside each icon. You may prefer having text "
"under each icon. You can also have plain texts without any icons or icons "
"only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3239
#, no-c-format
msgid "Icon Size"
msgstr "Talhas de las icònas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the size of the icons. Make your choice between small, "
"medium, large and huge icons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lock Toolbar Position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you unlock a toolbar, you can move the toolbar at the top, bottom, left, "
"right side or even outside the main &korganizer; window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3274
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&korganizer; provides you the possibility of extending the application with "
"plugins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The plugins can be configured under the &korganizer; main configuration "
"dialog. Choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem> "
"Configure &korganizer;</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and click the "
"<guilabel>Plugins</guilabel> icon on the icon list sidebar of the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3286
#, no-c-format
msgid "Available Plugins"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3289
#, no-c-format
msgid "Date Numbers Plugin for Calendars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This plugin adds the day number of day in the year to the agenda view. For "
"instance, February 1 is the day number 32."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3297
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wikipedia 'This Day in History' Plugin"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This plugin provides links to Wikipedia's <quote>This Day in History</quote> "
"pages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3304
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wikipedia Picture of the Day Plugin for Calendars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3305
#, no-c-format
msgid "This plugin provides the Wikipedia <quote>Picture of the Day</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3311
#, no-c-format
msgid "Jewish Calendar Plugin"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The plugin provides you Jewish calendar dates in addition to the Gregorian "
"calendar dates. In the configuration dialog of the plugin, you can choose if "
"you want to display Israeli holidays, weekly prasha, day of Omer and / or "
"Chol HaMoed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3321
#, no-c-format
msgid "Journal Print Style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3322
#, no-c-format
msgid "The plugin allows you to print out journal entries (diary entries)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3328
#, no-c-format
msgid "Yearly Print Style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3329
#, no-c-format
msgid "The plugin allows you to print out a yearly calendar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3339
#, no-c-format
msgid "Reference"
msgstr "Preferéncias"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3342
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menus"
msgstr "Menuts"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3344
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &korganizer; starts, the main &korganizer; window appears. The window "
"has several components: a menubar, a toolbar, a month calendar, a main panel "
"with the current <quote>view</quote> of events, and a to-do list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The menus provide access to all the common operations that can be performed "
"with the calendar, including saving, loading, adding and deleting events, to-"
"dos and journal entries, printing and more."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3353
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please note that when using &korganizer; as the calendar component of "
"&kontact;, the menus differ from the stand alone application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:3357
#, no-c-format
msgid "File"
msgstr "Fichièr"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3359
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>File</guimenu> menu provides access to functions involving the "
"entire calendar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:3395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>O</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu> File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Open</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3402
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Opens a file dialog allowing you to select a new vCalendar or "
"iCalendar file to load.</action> If you have made changes to the current "
"calendar, you will be given the option of saving them before loading a new "
"one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3406
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information about this, please refer to <xref linkend=\"managing-"
"import-export\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:3476
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu> File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Print</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose <guimenuitem>Print</guimenuitem> or click the <guilabel>Print</"
"guilabel> icon to <action>print the current calendar</action>. You can "
"specify the range of dates to be printed (either manually or with Calendar "
"Widget) and the Print Style (Day, Week, Month or To-dos and Journal)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:3493
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu> File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Print Preview</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3497
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you choose <guimenuitem>Print Preview</guimenuitem> or click the "
"<guiicon>Print Preview</guiicon> icon, <action>the current calendar will be "
"printed on your screen, instead of on your printer</action>. Use this "
"feature to check if the printout will be correct before you start printing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3502
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can specify the range of dates to be printed (either manually or with "
"Calendar Widget) and the View Type (Day, Week, Month or To-do)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:3508
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Import</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Import "
"Calendar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have a different iCalendar or vCalendar file somewhere, and you would "
"like to <action>merge its contents into your own calendar, add as a new "
"resource or open it as a new window</action>, choose this menu item. A good "
"time to do this would be if you received a vCalendar with a few entries via "
"email, for instance."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3518 index.docbook:3536
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information about this action, please refer to <xref linkend="
"\"managing-import\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:3524
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Import</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Import "
"From &UNIX; Ical Tool</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3529
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have used <application>ical</application>, a popular but older "
"calendar program for &UNIX;, you may wish to <action>import your events and "
"to-do</action> directly to &korganizer;. This action will read the "
"<filename>.calendar</filename> file from your home folder and merge any "
"entries it contains into your current calendar. If any errors or suspicious "
"things occur during the process, you will be notified via a message box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:3542
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Import</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Get Hot "
"New Stuff...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This action will open the <guilabel>Get Hot New Stuff</guilabel> dialog, "
"which offers a list of calendars to download. These events can be added to "
"your calendar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3550
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information about this action, please refer to <xref linkend="
"\"managing-get-hot-new-stuff\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:3556
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Export</guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Export "
"Web Page...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: action
#: index.docbook:3561
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can export your calendar or a part of it as a &HTML; file, suitable for "
"publishing on the World Wide Web."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3563 index.docbook:3576 index.docbook:3590
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information about this action, please refer to <xref linkend="
